.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH terminal-of-tinsel 1  "terminal-of-tinsel 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
terminal\-of\-tinsel \- Channel 25\*(Aqs Midwinter Special: the creatures of Christmas folklore, live in your terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBterminal\-of\-tinsel\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-pack\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] [\fIsubcommands\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Terminal of Tinsel brings the creatures of Christmas folklore to your terminal: St Nicholas\*(Aqs grim companions, the Yule Cat and the Yule Lads, the Mari Lwyd at the door and the spirits of A Christmas Carol, presented by your host, Auntie Aerial, live on Channel 25\*(Aqs Midwinter Special.
.PP
Start here:  terminal\-of\-tinsel creature
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the command\*(Aqs data as JSON instead of drawing it (errors become a JSON object on stderr)
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Plain output: no colour, no emoji, ASCII borders (also set by NO_COLOR, or by piping)
.TP
\fB\-\-pack\fR \fI<PACK>\fR
Only use creatures from these packs, e.g. \-\-pack nordic,dickens
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-list(1)
List every creature, grouped by pack
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-creature(1)
Tune in to the Midwinter Special, or read one creature\*(Aqs page
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-random(1)
A random creature fact, or with \-\-daily the Fact of the Night
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-quiz(1)
Pull a cracker: the Christmas Cracker Quiz
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-guess(1)
Guess the Guest: name the creature behind the frosted window
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-mash(1)
The Snowball Showdown: pit two creatures against each other
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-stocking(1)
Look in your stocking: the creatures you\*(Aqve caught, your badges and records
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-tonight(1)
See tonight\*(Aqs Christmas double bill
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-countdown(1)
Count the sleeps until Christmas
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-advent(1)
Open the advent calendar: a different guest behind each door
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-packs(1)
List the packs of creatures, or make your own
.TP
terminal\-of\-tinsel\-completions(1)
Print a shell completion script
.SH EXTRA
Set NO_COLOR or pass \-\-no\-color for plain output. Every command takes \-\-json.
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
